From: openEuler package maintenance <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read pending bytes or EOF when poll reports input hangup

A pipe writer can close after its last bytes have been consumed. poll then
reports POLLHUP, not POLLIN. Reading that ready descriptor obtains EOF and
allows the existing drain-and-finish condition to terminate mode 4 normally.
Preserve all buffer, output, throughput and byte-limit logic.

--- a/cstream.c
+++ b/cstream.c
@@ -1375,7 +1375,7 @@
       curwrite += ret;
     }
 
-    if (want_to_read && pollfd[0].revents & (POLLIN|POLLRDNORM)) {
+    if (want_to_read && pollfd[0].revents & (POLLIN|POLLRDNORM|POLLHUP)) {
       if (o->v >= 4)
 	fprintf(stderr, "Trying to read\n");
 
